-- title:
--   Degree-one place above a root pair of Φₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let `data` be a modular-polynomial datum of level $p$: a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic in $Y$, of degree $\sum_{d \mid p,\ d \text{ squarefree}} p/d$ in $Y$, and satisfies $\Phi = 0$ after substituting the $q$-expansion $j(q)$ for $X$ and the expansion `jqN p` for $Y$ in Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $j_1, j_2$ be elements of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and assume $\Phi$ vanishes when its inner coefficient polynomials are evaluated at $j_1$ and the outer variable at $j_2$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a place $x$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — that is, of the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the latter being the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $p$ — where a place is a proper valuation subring containing the image of the constant field and which is a principal ideal ring, such that: the residue field of $x$ has degree $1$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and both $\mathrm{ord}_x(\bar{j} - j_1) > 0$ and $\mathrm{ord}_x(\bar{j}_p - j_2) > 0$, where $\bar{j}$ is the image of $j(q)$, $\bar{j}_p$ the image of $j(q^p)$ (the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ on exponents), the constants $j_1, j_2$ are taken via the structure map, and $\mathrm{ord}_x$ is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation.
--
--   This is the place-attachment step in the moduli dictionary for Mazur's Step 3: since the function field of $X_0(p)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is generated by $j$ and $j_p$ subject to $\Phi_p(j, j_p) = 0$, every root pair of $\Phi_p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a closed point of the affine model and is therefore reached by a degree-one place at which $j - j_1$ and $j_p - j_2$ both vanish. It is used to produce moduli points from pairs consisting of a Weierstrass curve and a subgroup, in [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.existsUnique_place_centred_hasValue_nodeCoord`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.existsUnique_place_centred_hasValue_nodeCoord) and [`ModularCurve.moduliPointExists_jQuotVelu_of_mult_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.moduliPointExists_jQuotVelu_of_mult_two).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_place_of_modularPolynomial_eval_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib
